&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://ci.ignite.apache.org/viewLog.html?buildId=3506829&amp;amp;buildTypeId=IgniteTests24Java8_RunAll&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;TeamCity &lt;b&gt;--&amp;gt; Run :: All&lt;/b&gt; Results&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16812201" author="vozerov" created="Mon, 8 Apr 2019 07:56:39 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=amashenkov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;amashenkov&quot;&gt;amashenkov&lt;/a&gt;, my comments:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;IgniteH2Indexing&lt;/tt&gt; - unused import&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;CacheMvccSqlTxModesTest&lt;/tt&gt; - we need more tests here. Original problem was that we if there are both MVCC and non-MVCC caches, then OPTIMISTIC transactions on non-MVCC caches were not possible. Let&apos;s add a set of tests ensuring that all combinations of isolation/concurrency are possible on non-MVCC caches in presence of MVCC cache, and that all PESSIMISTIC modes (READ_COMMITTED, REPEATABLE_READ, SERIALIZABLE) are supported for MVCC caches.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;I would propose to rename new public exceptions a bit, so that they start with &quot;Transaction&quot; word. For example:
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;NonMvccTransactionException&lt;/tt&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;tt&gt;TransactionMixedModeException&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;&lt;tt&gt;UnsupportedTxModeException&lt;/tt&gt; -&amp;gt; &lt;tt&gt;TransactionUnsupportedConcurrencyException&lt;/tt&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
</comment>
